\f0\fs22 \cf2 \CocoaLigature0  Build's good. Here's the calibration walkthrough for when you're back at the\
  installation:\
\
  
\f1\b 1. Turn on the webcam preview
\f0\b0 \
\
  In the bottom control bar of the app:\
  1. Click the 
\f1\b camera icon
\f0\b0  to turn on webcam tracking. Your browser will ask for\
  camera permission \'97 click Allow. \
  2. A new 
\f1\b crosshair icon
\f0\b0  appears next to it. Click that to open the "Webcam\
  Calibration" box in the bottom-right corner of the screen.\
  \
  You'll now see a small video preview of what the laptop's webcam sees, plus\
  some text below it.\
\
  
\f1\b 2. Set up the laptop
\f0\b0 \
  \
  Open the laptop and place it at one edge of the floor area, screen facing into\
  the space, so the webcam can see the whole area people will walk around in.\
  It doesn't need to be perfectly aimed \'97 you'll calibrate around wherever it\
  ends up.\
\
  
\f1\b 3. Calibrate left/right (\cf3 camMinX\cf2  / \cf3 camMaxX\cf2 )
\f0\b0 \
\
  I added a live readout to make this purely "read a number, write it down" \'97 no\
  need to judge positions visually.\
\
  1. Stand at whichever edge of the floor area you want to correspond to the\
  
\f1\b left side
\f0\b0  of the projection.\
  2. Look at the calibration box. Under the video, you'll see a line like:\
  \cf3 left/right: 0.XXX (currently left=0.15, right=0.85)\cf2 \
  3. Write down that number. This will become your new \cf3 camMinX\cf2 .\
  4. Now walk to the edge that should correspond to the 
\f1\b right side
\f0\b0  of the\
  projection.\
  5. Write down the new \cf3 left/right\cf2  number. This becomes your new \cf3 camMaxX\cf2 .\
\
  Don't worry about which number is bigger \'97 just write down whatever you see at\
  each spot.\
  \
  
\f1\b 4. Calibrate near/far (\cf3 camNearTorso\cf2  / \cf3 camFarTorso\cf2 )
\f0\b0 \
\
  Same idea, second line of the readout:\
  \cf3 near/far: 0.XXX (currently near=0.35, far=0.12)\cf2 \
\
  1. Stand at the spot 
\f1\b closest to the camera
\f0\b0  that people would realistically\
  stand. Write down the \cf3 near/far\cf2  number \'97 this becomes \cf3 camNearTorso\cf2 .\
  2. Stand at the spot 
\f1\b farthest from the camera
\f0\b0 . Write down that number \'97 this\
  becomes \cf3 camFarTorso\cf2 .\
\
  This number is just "how tall your torso looks" \'97 naturally bigger when you're\
  close, smaller when you're far. You don't need to think about it beyond\
  "stand here, write the number down."\
  \
  
\f1\b 5.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Enter
\f0\b0  
\f1\b the
\f0\b0  
\f1\b numbers
\f0\b0 \
\
  Open \cf3 src/useMediaPipePose.js\cf2 . Near the top (around lines 20 and 29-30) you'll\
  see:\
\
  \cf4 export\cf2  \cf4 const\cf2  camMinX = \cf5 0.15\cf2 ;\
  \cf4 export\cf2  \cf4 const\cf2  camMaxX = \cf5 0.85\cf2 ;\
  ...\
  \cf4 export\cf2  \cf4 const\cf2  camNearTorso = \cf5 0.35\cf2 ;\
  \cf4 export\cf2  \cf4 const\cf2  camFarTorso = \cf5 0.12\cf2 ;\
  \
  Replace each with the number you wrote down in the matching spot (left \uc0\u8594 \
  \cf3 camMinX\cf2 , right \uc0\u8594  \cf3 camMaxX\cf2 , near \uc0\u8594  \cf3 camNearTorso\cf2 , far \uc0\u8594  \cf3 camFarTorso\cf2 ). Save the\
  file.\
  \
  
\f1\b 6.
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Test
\f0\b0 \
\
  If running \cf3 npm run dev\cf2 , the page should reload automatically. Walk around the\
  floor \'97 moving side to side should move the highlighted sound side to side,\
  and moving toward/away from the camera should move it correspondingly. If one\
  axis feels reversed or cramped, just repeat steps 3-4 (or 4 alone) and try\
  again \'97 it's just two numbers per axis, so it's quick to redo.\
\
  One tip: do this with only yourself in frame (not a second person), so the\
  numbers in the readout are unambiguous.}